Core's protections below apply as soon as you confirm, and approval for every
command from each pane's next turn. From then until the restart, also: approved
and allow-listed commands stay inside this session's sandbox (commands can write
to the current folder, /private/tmp) and network is off for agent commands.
The rest of the rows above take effect when you restart Corbanu Terminal (you
can restart right after saving); until then this session keeps its current
settings for the rest, apart from Core's protected-path denials, and commands
already running keep the permissions they started with. Your config.toml is
not modified.
